  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.5.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: marimo-jupyter-extension\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/m/marimo-jupyter-extension/marimo_jupyter_extension-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: be262d6b39ab8eb655d9e736a0f707a31a09712f0229bb7dc2aa0e0f53c82469\n  patches:\n    # conda-forge's uv is the standalone binary without Python dist-info, so\n    # pip check would fail on the 'uv' wheel requirement. The extension only\n    # shells out to uv/uvx and never imports the uv module, so drop it from the\n    # wheel metadata and keep uv as a conda run requirement instead.\n    - drop-uv-wheel-requirement.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - hatchling\n    - jupyterlab >=4.0.0,<5\n    - hatch-jupyter-builder\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - jupyter-server-proxy\n    - traitlets >=5.0\n    - tomlkit >=0.12.0\n    - uv >=0.4\n    - nbconvert >=7.0\n    - packaging\n    - pyzmq\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - marimo_jupyter_extension\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n\nabout:\n  summary: Jupyter extension to proxy marimo with JupyterLab integration\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - NOTICE\n  homepage: https://github.com/marimo-team/marimo-jupyter-extension\n  repository: https://github.com/marimo-team/marimo-jupyter-extension\n  documentation: https://marimo-team.github.io/marimo-jupyter-extension/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - dmadisetti\n",
